ref 17592186481528} {:answer/id #uuid "f44e1dc0-ddc5-5eaf-a71d-4d2449aa8967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = -3x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f82bade-02b4-5fbf-a007-72dbcc424105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3x + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481511} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc177dac-11d2-54e1-bf1c-b70a22275365" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481526}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5797ea3-bc2d-51fe-9adc-fde728d4e47d" :question/problem "![](images/95/95f066686cfcee7d1bbb9c451bd6ea007c8bb5433bee6eda06f886d241280180.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y = 3x + 3$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = 3x + 3\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = 3x + 3\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n3\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $3$ that passes through the point $(0,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (1) &= 3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny &= 3x + (1) \\\\\ny &= 3x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d21854e5-c76d-59bc-87eb-08b5c002fa75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d21854e5-c76d-59bc-87eb-08b5c002fa75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481532} :answer-field/id #uuid "7812f2c1-a5b3-503d-a754-6cf928ad7d6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc76128b-1dbf-5fe8-8ff5-5650472a624c" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e73ff4c357b70c3c740666cab209f33cf08236f9244f044009905a6123cff6b4.png)\n\nThe equation of the line $l_{1}$ is $y =-\\frac{3}{2}x$ and the line $l_{2}$ is parallel to $l_{1}$. What is the equation of $l_{2}$?$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, the slope of the new line should be equal to the slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, we want a line with the slope $-\\frac{3}{2}$ that passes through the point $(-2,1)$. Using point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (1) &= -\\frac{3}{2}(x - (-2)) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{2}x - 3 + (1) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{2}x - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Passing Through a Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175911 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175738 :question/id #uuid "8d4fd310-7de4-5498-9473-68c1a61fde46" :question/math-academy-id "e-14368" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(1,-1)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(3,1)$ and $(6,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(3,1)$ and $(6,2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 - 1}{6 - 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(1,-1)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1) \\\\\ny + 1 &= \\frac{1}{3}x - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{1}{3}x - \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fded3d63-be68-5e3e-b633-58d282d16ef2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049061 :topic/math-academy-id 396 :topic/title "Calculating Slopes of Straight Lines"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "f806eee8-5621-511c-8bbe-af7e6d6049ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174744}] :question/id #uuid "e8eddceb-6f73-589d-b9db-631e5d4c9331" :question/math-academy-id "q-214094" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(1, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(4, 3)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "c787dd1f-b191-5f32-9814-5edd8b722d19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174748}] :question/id #uuid "692ddd92-50e1-5acb-a7bd-1f6656bd869f" :question/math-academy-id "q-216200" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, 2)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3,-1)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb37d251-78c1-585a-a212-8a9675670642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb37d251-78c1-585a-a212-8a9675670642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487511} :answer-field/id #uuid "754bd463-955e-57d8-bbcc-0b7dc5c963cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487497}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b3f609e-5f7c-5214-b10a-b8eb08f476e6" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, 0)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-1\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -1(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -x \\\\\ny &= 3 -x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96cb51b2-2c7c-5a26-b048-f979dc22c48b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96cb51b2-2c7c-5a26-b048-f979dc22c48b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487500} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c0fa8f-73b1-568e-8887-368007009980" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487486}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26ebeaaf-47b4-5e9b-a15e-2fa9e9b6c345" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, 2)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, 3)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n2\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,2)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (2) &= 2(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (2) &= 2 x \\\\\ny &= 2 x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5576b774-72b2-5132-a278-f30180c12f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{3} -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5576b774-72b2-5132-a278-f30180c12f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{3} -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487493} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc7c5f0-0290-5fb8-b2f4-9db06328fc20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487496}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2865c105-cc26-596d-8d65-cb20c88dfa23" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-3, -4)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(5, -2)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(5,-2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-2 - (-1)}{5 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(-3,-4)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-4) &= -\\frac{1}{3}(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - (-4) &= -\\frac{x}{3} -1 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{x}{3} -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dcf6f39-4305-56d2-80f5-d536e4837322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 x -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dcf6f39-4305-56d2-80f5-d536e4837322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 x -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487495} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe781696-c521-5458-a85f-750018644896" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487514}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e11ebc7-3a29-5e32-9ded-4e8408b30cb8" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, -1)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, -2)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,-2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-2 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-3\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,-1)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= -3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= -3 x \\\\\ny &= -3 x -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f05d5dc-1f1f-5341-bed0-2a40038347de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 -\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f05d5dc-1f1f-5341-bed0-2a40038347de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 -\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487491} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9db8c26-61f5-5a2d-9290-3fd2495a2f22" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "845f9834-f22b-53bc-a424-04017a3a9353" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(3, 4)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(5, -2)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(5,-2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-2 - (-1)}{5 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(3,4)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (4) &= -\\frac{1}{3}(x - (3)) \\\\\ny - (4) &= 1 -\\frac{x}{3} \\\\\ny &= 5 -\\frac{x}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53c1a7d8-d707-510e-b92d-9a1719bf5638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53c1a7d8-d707-510e-b92d-9a1719bf5638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487492} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b193b39-1715-5634-9926-b73db7bc4c8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487499}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "998bca3d-674e-50cd-9fff-229848ef3e23" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-3, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(4, 0)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(4,0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0 - (-1)}{4 - (2)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(-3,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{1}{2}(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3b1e17e-b281-5dda-86ff-43b200f959e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3b1e17e-b281-5dda-86ff-43b200f959e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487510} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2d46d7-e9a5-5f5a-8dc6-05b51f351ec5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e690e28-5baa-55f2-888d-294c615d87b1" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, 4)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, -1)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,-1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-1 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-2\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,4)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (4) &= -2(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (4) &= -2 x \\\\\ny &= 4 -2 x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "629e4a61-587c-549d-96ab-2d80c984c89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 x -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "629e4a61-587c-549d-96ab-2d80c984c89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 x -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487494} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa771f7e-6c97-5c4c-a502-705e8ad82076" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aff5cd8f-a493-573f-8242-c9b1643ca3ab" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, -1)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, 4)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n3\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,-1)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= 3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= 3 x \\\\\ny &= 3 x -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be6f683-a283-589c-bceb-049b76002cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x}{3} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9be6f683-a283-589c-bceb-049b76002cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x}{3} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487502} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f3f9e90-ab11-5f72-a9d3-673d96f460e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487489}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbd313e5-081f-50f3-9aa3-de2e999a214f" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-3, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(5, 1)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(5,1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - (-1)}{5 - (2)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(-3,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{2}{3}(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{2 x}{3} + 2 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2 x}{3} + 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0bcaabb-3c95-55ba-9dcf-7a35953d4082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0bcaabb-3c95-55ba-9dcf-7a35953d4082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487509} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74f997c-c7cd-5d70-89ae-414d8a64d72a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487513}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ebcde1e1-9558-5044-b7d6-26cd0859557b" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(1, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(4, -3)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(4,-3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-3 - (-1)}{4 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-1\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(1,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -1(x - (1)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= 1 -x \\\\\ny &= 4 -x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Passing Through Two Points"}]}
